The experimental Camxes-JS parser=20
<http://mw.lojban.org/extensions/ilmentufa/camxes-exp.html> I initiated=20
was by no mean intended to represent the official grammar of Lojban or=20
any upgrade thereof; the experimental Camxes is there for testing=20
implementations of various grammar change proposals, in order to check=20
whether they are compatible with PEG or conflict with some other parts=20
of the grammar, a little like a sandbox grammar; some of these changes=20
might be approved to be part of official Lojban in the future, and=20
others are either unlikely to be approved or are highly controversial.

The experimental Camxes-JS was thus by no mean intended to be able to=20
parse the story called {la .teris.}. :-)

The official version of Camxes-JS=20
<http://mw.lojban.org/extensions/ilmentufa/camxes.html> should comply=20
with whatever decisions the BPFK makes with regard to the grammar, and=20
be updated accordingly. If you want to parse a text using the official=20
grammar, please use the official version of Camxes-JS, and not the=20
experimental version thereof.

As for other common dialects, they'd need their own dedicated parser,=20
and I approve of Guskant's initiative to make Zantufa parsers for=20
several of these dialects (for example the one used in The Wonderful=20
Wizard of Oz, which uses the Brivla-Cmevla Merger).

mi'e la .ilmen. mu'o


